{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s28-p01",
      "text": "People know animals do have feelings.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p02",
      "text": "Scientists have done research about the feelings of cows, frogs and pandas.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p03",
      "text": "A new study adds chickens to the list.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p04-01",
      "text": "We know that during a storm with thunder and lightning,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p04-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p04-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p04-02",
      "text": "these animals get shocked and stay close together near the bottom of the barn.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p04-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p04-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p05",
      "text": "But what do they say?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p06-01",
      "text": "It seems that humans can tell whether hens and roosters are happy or sad by listening to their calls,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p06-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p06-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p06-02",
      "text": "just like hearing other people say \"hello\" or \"goodbye\" with different tones.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p06-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p06-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p07",
      "text": "The researchers put a bowl behind a door.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p08",
      "text": "Sometimes, there was something chickens love to eat in the bowl, such as rice, sweet porridge or insects.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p09",
      "text": "Sometimes, the bowl was empty.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p10-01",
      "text": "Chickens that saw food seemed happy and produced fast and loud sounds,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p10-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p10-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p10-02",
      "text": "which they also do when playing with a new toy.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p10-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p10-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p11",
      "text": "Chickens that saw an empty bowl made low and long noises to express disappointment.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p12",
      "text": "The researchers recorded all these sounds and studied their waves.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p13",
      "text": "The researchers played 16 recordings of such chicken noises to 194 volunteers.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p14",
      "text": "Half were from the chickens seeing the food, and half were from the chickens finding no food.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p15",
      "text": "Sixty-nine per cent of the volunteers correctly understood the chickens' emotions.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p16",
      "text": "The result shows that humans have the natural ability to understand the feelings of chickens.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p17-01",
      "text": "Hopefully, this finding can bring about new technology to help bosses of farms in raising chickens,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p17-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p17-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p17-02",
      "text": "a big industry in many countries.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p17-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p17-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p18",
      "text": "Scientists are working on a smart computer program that can identify chickens' feelings.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28-p19",
      "text": "Good news for farmers who want to make the birds happier and healthier.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s28-p19.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
